#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:10
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Hatókör"

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 12 application modules and 4,449 lines (43,721 measured"
" proxy tokens): confirmation blockers and records, confirmation-field "
"resolution, consent withdrawal survey, remembered counterparty facts and "
"registered access, country-vocabulary advisories, deterministic checks, "
"direction suggestion, in-memory transcription, and the counterparty "
"establishment ladder. All assigned ranges were read in eight bounded "
"pages. This is static inspection; it does not validate legal content, "
"execute persistence adapters, or prove the wider confirmation workflow "
"invokes every local service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:14
msgid "Human confirmation and retained evidence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:16
msgid ""
"The confirmation gate turns deterministic discrepancies and ambiguous "
"identity fields into stable, content-derived blockers. Every discrepancy "
"kind maps to a blocking reason, and an import-time completeness check "
"refuses to load if that mapping is incomplete. The gate rejects unknown "
"blocker IDs, duplicate answers, unanswered findings, and candidate "
"choices that were not offered by the draft. Candidate identity values may"
" be named by the rendered digest, allowing a reviewer to answer without "
"the raw value crossing the review surface. ATTEST requires a note; value-"
"bearing actions require a nonblank value. There is no bulk “accept all” "
"route in this gate. Blocker coverage and IDs "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_gate.py`) Finding "
"resolution shape (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_gate.py`) "
"Per-finding gate (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_gate.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:18
msgid ""
"On confirmation, `FieldAssertion` preserves the operator’s supplied value"
" beside the prior reading, its origin, and grounding. The draft’s "
"provenance for an overridden field is replaced by an unanchored OPERATOR "
"envelope; it is not left appearing as a document reading. "
"`InvoiceConfirmationRecord` stores who/when, evidence and transcription "
"content digests when available, extractor identity, assertions, resolved "
"blockers, and the names of deterministic checks run. Its persisted record"
" uses a bucket-scoped document, and a duplicate derived ID returns the "
"already stored record. Assertion and record types "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_record.py`) Record writing "
"and duplicate behavior "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_record.py`) Assertions and "
"re-stamping (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_record.py`) "
"Record construction "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_record.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:20
msgid ""
"The record ID deserves a scoped follow-up: its hash covers bucket, "
"invoice ID, evidence reference, actor, assertions, and resolved blocker "
"pairs, but omits the stored evidence SHA-256, transcription SHA-256, and "
"extractor revision. Since the writer returns the old row on a matching ID"
" without comparing those omitted fields, safety depends on the evidence "
"reference and outcome being the intended idempotency boundary (for "
"example, if references are immutable). Trace the caller and evidence-"
"store identity guarantees; otherwise a reused reference with changed "
"bytes or reader revision could return stale provenance. The "
"read/append/save protocol also has no revision witness in this module, so"
" confirm that its adapter or enclosing operation prevents lost updates "
"under concurrent confirmations. Derived-ID inputs "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_record.py`) Duplicate "
"short-circuit and repository contract "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_record.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:22
msgid ""
"Confirmed-field resolvers layer a supplied operator value over the draft "
"reading, refuse required fields that neither side supplies, select date-"
"sensitive domestic rate tiers without approximating multi-rate or recargo"
" cases, and preserve per-rate breakdown lines when the operator has not "
"restated the totals. This is pure resolution; writing remains in the "
"caller. Field precedence and required-field refusal "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmed_field_resolution.py`) Dated "
"rate-tier decision "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmed_field_resolution.py`) Invoice "
"line preservation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmed_field_resolution.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:24
msgid "Counterparty facts and territorial resolution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:26
msgid ""
"An operator may persist a counterparty’s territorial establishment and/or"
" IVA-identification state under a digest of a canonical verified tax "
"identifier; the raw identifier stays in the encrypted fact payload rather"
" than the storage object key. The two facts are independent, and records "
"must answer at least one. Confirmed facts are operator assertions only. A"
" conflicting assertion is refused rather than silently replacing an "
"answer; adding a previously unanswered identification state is permitted;"
" removing a fact is a distinct operation. Resolution compares a stored "
"territory with current document evidence and returns neither side as "
"usable when they disagree. Hashed counterparty key "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/counterparty_establishment.py`) Stored-"
"fact invariants "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/counterparty_establishment.py`) "
"Record/update and conflict policy "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/counterparty_establishment.py`) Lookup "
"and contradiction "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/counterparty_establishment.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:28
msgid ""
"The registered counterparty operation offers confirm, view, and withdraw "
"under exact-profile access. View is read-only; mutations require COMMIT "
"and run inside an irreversible section with an UNKNOWN effect before "
"repository work. It validates scope and Member-State values through the "
"pinned authority and reports whether storage changed. Request shape "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/counterparty_operation.py`) Executor "
"effects and actions "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/counterparty_operation.py`) Access and "
"registration (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/counterparty_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:30
msgid ""
"For document confirmation, the establishment ladder checks whether a "
"foreign IVA registration conflicts with evidence placing the counterparty"
" in Spain, then considers the address country, Spanish postal code only "
"when Spain was named, treatment concordant with non-establishment, and "
"finally a remembered operator fact. A foreign tax prefix by itself "
"establishes registration, not territorial location. Country/postal/rate "
"lookups are date- and registry-backed; unknown or absent evidence "
"produces no default territory. A remembered scope is compared even when "
"the document is decisive, so conflicting facts return a contradiction "
"rather than allowing one source to silently win. Rung and evidence policy"
" (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/establishment_ladder.py`) Ordered "
"evidence walk (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/establishment_ladder.py`) "
"Store comparison and fallback "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/establishment_ladder.py`) Draft-to-"
"counterparty routing "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/establishment_ladder.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:32
msgid ""
"Country codes that are well-formed but outside the shipped vocabulary, or"
" reserved as unassigned, produce a nonblocking advisory when no other "
"country evidence already settles the territory. The notice distinguishes "
"a likely document placeholder from a gap in the application’s vocabulary."
" This warning does not supply a scope; classification still refuses if a "
"required territory cannot be established. Country warning policy "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/country_vocabulary_advisory.py`) "
"Advisory decision "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/country_vocabulary_advisory.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:34
msgid ""
"Direction derivation compares the filer's identifier against the "
"supplier/customer tax-ID slots, then requires the value to occur inside "
"exactly that party’s heading region in the independent transcription. It "
"returns a suggestion only; it does not mutate the draft or override the "
"operator’s confirmed direction. If the filer is absent/on both sides, "
"headings are unavailable, or containment is ambiguous, it explains that "
"direction was not settled. Direction states and derivation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/document_direction.py`) Role-containment"
" rule (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/document_direction.py`) Suggestion"
" entrypoint (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/document_direction.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:36
msgid "Privacy, safety, and implementation assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:38
msgid ""
"`DocumentTranscription` carries verbatim reading-order financial text in "
"memory with source-content digest and transcriber provenance. Its text is"
" excluded from `repr`, and Pydantic serialization, iteration, and "
"pickling deliberately raise, so accidental model persistence fails rather"
" than exporting readable invoice contents. The required transport and "
"reader revision distinguish where and how the text was produced. "
"Transcriber provenance "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/document_transcription.py`) In-memory "
"transcription protections "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/document_transcription.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:40
msgid ""
"Consent withdrawal is transparent that transmitted bytes cannot be "
"recalled. It requires the caller to supply consent-ledger entries, "
"filters them to the selected profile, and separately lists persisted "
"drafts whose transport is nonlocal or unknown (empty transport fails open"
" to inclusion). It surveys stored extraction drafts; completeness of off-"
"host history depends on the injected consent-ledger projection and the "
"set of persisted artefacts this store exposes. In this projection, "
"`provenance_stamp` is populated from `stored.extractor`; verify the "
"stored record’s semantics before treating that field name as a complete "
"provenance envelope. Transport selection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/consent_withdrawal.py`) Withdrawal "
"survey (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/consent_withdrawal.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:42
msgid ""
"The deterministic-check registry runs the same draft-only checks through "
"one list and derives the recorded check names from that list; this "
"reduces drift between what ran and what a confirmation claims ran. Its "
"checks include closure, regime contradiction, and postal-code shape. The "
"findings are blocking, while vocabulary/advisory-only conditions remain "
"outside the blocking discrepancy axis. Check declaration and names "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/deterministic_findings.py`) "
"Deterministic execution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/deterministic_findings.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-provenance.md:44
msgid ""
"The strongest local controls are explicit per-finding review, auditable "
"corrections, refusal to invent counterparty territory, separation of "
"registration from establishment, exact-profile mutation access, and "
"transcription custody tripwires. Confirm the confirmation caller applies "
"every supplied resolution to the intended draft fields before minting an "
"invoice: the gate proves a blocker was answered, while "
"`build_confirmation_record` pairs only resolutions present and relies on "
"its caller to have run the gate. The counterparty operations return tax "
"identifiers and notes in their result models, so check that the secure "
"operand and frontend projection remain the only route to those values. No"
" tests were inspected or run; current legal accuracy and production "
"adapter behavior are outside this static pass."
msgstr ""

